Copyright: subproject `OROneRel` -- one-relator combinatorics (node N2).

# The HNN step of the Freiheitssatz, and the induction interface

The Freiheitssatz is proved by strong induction on `relatorNorm`.  The induction step reduces to
`T = {a | a ≠ x}` for a letter `x` of the relator, cyclically rotates the relator so that it begins
with `x`, and then distinguishes whether some letter `t` of the relator has exponent sum zero.

* If `σ_t r = 0` then `⟨α | r⟩` is an HNN extension of the one-relator group
  `G' = ⟨(α \ {t}) × ℤ | r'⟩`, where `r' = magRewRel t r` is the Magnus rewriting of `r` with
  respect to `t` (deleting the `t`-letters and decorating the others by the running exponent sum of
  `t`), with stable letter `t`.  The interface to that decomposition is the structure
  `HNNStepCore r t x a b` below: it records the associated subgroups `A`, `B`, the isomorphism `φ`
  between them, and -- crucially for the Freiheitssatz -- the homomorphism
  `θ : ⟨α | r⟩ →* HNNExtension G' A B φ` which is injective and sends the generator `s ≠ t` to the
  base generator `(s,0)` and the generator `t` to the stable letter.

* If no letter of `r` has exponent sum zero, one substitutes `t ↦ t ^ (σ_x r)`,
  `x ↦ x * t ^ (-(σ_t r))` (and fixes all other letters) to reach the previous case; this is the
  content of `freiheitssatz_case2`.

The exponent-sum-zero case splits further: if `t ∈ T` one uses that a word `w ∈ F(T)` with
`σ_t w = 0` rewrites to a word in the generators other than `x` and `t`, for which the induction
hypothesis applies; if `t ∉ T` the induction hypothesis applies directly to the rewritten relator.
-/

import Mathlib
import Submission.Work.OROneRel.Interface
import Submission.Work.OROneRel.FreiheitssatzDefs

namespace Work.OROneRel

universe u

variable {α : Type u}

/-- **The induction hypothesis, uniformly over all generating types.**  `FreiheitssatzBelow N` is the
statement of the Freiheitssatz for every relator of norm `< N` over *every* generating type in the
universe `u`.  The type parameter is essential: the induction step passes from `α` to the rewriting
type `(α \ {t}) × ℤ`. -/
def FreiheitssatzBelow (N : ℕ) : Prop :=
  ∀ (β : Type u) (s : FreeGroup β), relatorNorm s < N → FreiheitssatzAt s

/-- The Magnus rewriting (with respect to the letter `t`) of a relator `w`, as an element of the free
group on `(α \ {t}) × ℤ`: the `t`-letters of `w` are deleted and each remaining letter is decorated
by the exponent sum of `t` in the preceding prefix. -/
noncomputable def magRewRel (t : α) (w : FreeGroup α) : FreeGroup ({a : α // a ≠ t} × ℤ) := by
  classical
  exact FreeGroup.mk (rewrite t w.toWord)

/-- The base group `G' = ⟨(α \ {t}) × ℤ | magRewRel t r⟩` of the HNN step. -/
abbrev HNNBase (r : FreeGroup α) (t : α) : Type u :=
  PresentedGroup ({magRewRel t r} : Set (FreeGroup ({a : α // a ≠ t} × ℤ)))

/-- The canonical map `G' →* HNNExtension G' A B φ`, with all arguments explicit (a name for
`HNNExtension.of`, so that statements can mention it without type ascriptions). -/
abbrev hnnOf (r : FreeGroup α) (t : α) {A B : Subgroup (HNNBase r t)} {phi : A ≃* B}
    (g : HNNBase r t) : HNNExtension (HNNBase r t) A B phi :=
  HNNExtension.of g

/-- The stable letter of the HNN extension `HNNExtension G' A B φ`, with all arguments explicit. -/
abbrev hnnT (r : FreeGroup α) (t : α) (A B : Subgroup (HNNBase r t)) (phi : A ≃* B) :
    HNNExtension (HNNBase r t) A B phi :=
  HNNExtension.t

/-- **The HNN step of the Freiheitssatz.**  Data exhibiting `⟨α | r⟩`, for a relator `r` with
`σ_t r = 0` whose word begins with `x` or `x⁻¹`, as an HNN extension of the one-relator group
`G' = ⟨(α \ {t}) × ℤ | r'⟩` (`r' = magRewRel t r`) with stable letter `t`.

The letter `x` controls the "strip" `S'` of generators of `G'` that occur in the decomposition: `a`
and `b` are the smallest and largest indices at which `x` occurs in `r'`, and the associated
subgroups `A`, `B` are generated by the same generators as `G'` except that the `x`-generators are
restricted to `a ≤ i ≤ b - 1` and `a + 1 ≤ i ≤ b` respectively; `φ` shifts the index by one.

Everything the Freiheitssatz argument consumes is recorded here: the injective map `θ` from
`⟨α | r⟩` into the HNN extension together with its values on the generators (`theta_of`, `theta_t`)
and the way the stable letter conjugates the base generators `(s,i)`, `s ≠ x` (`conj`). -/
structure HNNStepCore (r : FreeGroup α) (t x : α) (a b : ℤ) : Type u where
  /-- the first associated subgroup of the HNN decomposition (`x`-indices `a ≤ i ≤ b - 1`) -/
  A : Subgroup (HNNBase r t)
  /-- the second associated subgroup of the HNN decomposition (`x`-indices `a + 1 ≤ i ≤ b`) -/
  B : Subgroup (HNNBase r t)
  /-- the isomorphism between the associated subgroups, shifting the index by one -/
  phi : A ≃* B
  /-- the map from `⟨α | r⟩` to the HNN extension, injective -/
  theta : PresentedGroup ({r} : Set (FreeGroup α)) →* HNNExtension (HNNBase r t) A B phi
  /-- `θ` is injective: this is one half of the isomorphism `⟨α | r⟩ ≅ HNNExtension G' A B φ` -/
  theta_injective : Function.Injective theta
  /-- `θ` sends a generator `s ≠ t` to the corresponding base generator `(s, 0)` -/
  theta_of : ∀ (s : α) (hs : s ≠ t),
    theta (PresentedGroup.of s) =
      hnnOf r t (PresentedGroup.of ((⟨s, hs⟩, (0 : ℤ)) : ({a : α // a ≠ t} × ℤ)))
  /-- `θ` sends the generator `t` to the stable letter -/
  theta_t : theta (PresentedGroup.of t) = hnnT r t A B phi
  /-- conjugation by the stable letter raises the index of a generator `(s, i)`, `s ≠ x` -/
  conj : ∀ (s : α) (hs : s ≠ t) (hxs : s ≠ x) (i : ℤ),
    hnnT r t A B phi * hnnOf r t (PresentedGroup.of ((⟨s, hs⟩, i) : ({a : α // a ≠ t} × ℤ))) *
        (hnnT r t A B phi)⁻¹ =
      hnnOf r t (PresentedGroup.of ((⟨s, hs⟩, i + 1) : ({a : α // a ≠ t} × ℤ)))

/-- **The exponent-sum-zero engine.**  `ZeroExpsumEngine t x N` is the Freiheitssatz for every
cyclically reduced relator `s` with `σ_t s = 0` (so that `⟨α | s⟩` is an HNN extension with stable
letter `t` and base `⟨(α \ {t}) × ℤ | magRewRel t s⟩`, and the letter `x` controls the strip), for
every set `T'` of generators that does not generate `s`, provided either `x ∉ T'` (so that a word
of `F(T')` with exponent sum zero rewrites without `x`-letters) or `t ∉ T'` (so that `T'` lies in
the base).  The hypothesis `relatorNorm (magRewRel t s) < N` together with the induction hypothesis
`FreiheitssatzBelow N` supplies the Freiheitssatz at the HNN base. -/
def ZeroExpsumEngine (t x : α) (N : ℕ) : Prop :=
  ∀ (s : FreeGroup α) (T' : Set α), IsCyclicallyReducedRelator s → t ∈ relatorLetters s →
    x ∈ relatorLetters s → sigma t s = 1 → (x ∉ T' ∨ t ∉ T') →
    s ∉ Subgroup.closure (FreeGroup.of '' T') → relatorNorm (magRewRel t s) < N →
    FreiheitssatzBelow.{u} N → Function.Injective (presentedGroupMap s T')

/-- The substitution of Case 2 of the Freiheitssatz: `t ↦ t ^ p`, `x ↦ x * t ^ (-q)`, all other
letters fixed. -/
noncomputable def substFun (t x : α) (p q : ℤ) : α → FreeGroup α := by
  classical
  exact fun a =>
    if a = t then (FreeGroup.of t) ^ p
    else if a = x then FreeGroup.of x * (FreeGroup.of t) ^ (-q)
    else FreeGroup.of a

/-- The homomorphism of `F α` induced by the substitution of Case 2. -/
noncomputable def subst (t x : α) (p q : ℤ) : FreeGroup α →* FreeGroup α :=
  FreeGroup.lift (substFun t x p q)

end Work.OROneRel
